  (obj out dac~ (pos 20 720))
  (obj s2 comment "2. The transport is the patch's clock. There is one for the whole patch: every transport box (this one and the one at the top) shows and drives it, every score" (pos 20 765))
  (obj s2b comment "   plays on it. play, stop, rewind, locate a bar (and a beat), loop bars. tempo and meter change how bars and beats are counted (the numbers, locate, loop)," (pos 20 783))
  (obj s2c comment "   not the music: a score's times are seconds. Try tempo 60: the bars are twice as long, the tune keeps its pace; loop 1 3 now holds all four of its bars." (pos 20 801))
  (obj p2 message play (pos 20 830))
  (obj st2 message stop (pos 65 830))
  (obj rw2 message rewind (pos 110 830))
  (obj l3 message "locate 3" (pos 170 830))
  (obj l33 message "locate 3 3" (pos 240 830))
  (obj lp13 message "loop 1 3" (pos 320 830))
  (obj lp0 message "loop 0" (pos 390 830))
  (obj t60 message "tempo 60" (pos 450 830))
  (obj t120 message "tempo 120" (pos 520 830))
  (obj m34 message "meter 3 4" (pos 600 830))
  (obj m44 message "meter 4 4" (pos 680 830))
  (obj tr2 transport 120 4 4 (pos 20 865))
  (obj bar number (pos 20 900))
  (obj beat number (pos 90 900))
  (obj cbb comment "bar, beat (at every beat while it plays)" (pos 160 901))
  (obj s3 comment "3. The box is a roll: a staff a row, time to the right, a note a head and a line as long as it lasts. With the patch locked, click a note and drag it later or higher;" (pos 20 940))
  (obj s3b comment "   drag its end to make it longer; Alt-drag copies it; a rectangle selects several; Delete takes them out; the arrows nudge them (Shift: a bar, an octave)." (pos 20 958))
  (obj s3c comment "   Edit > Undo takes an edit back (the box clicked last). Play while you edit: every edit is heard at once. In edit mode the box's corner sizes it." (pos 20 976))
  (obj s4 comment "4. One score, four views. Double-click the box: its window. At its top: Roll (staves), Piano roll (pitch up, time right), List (an event a line) and Timeline (tracks)." (pos 20 1008))
  (obj s4b comment "   They are views of the same score: switch, and the selection and the playhead stay; an edit in one is in all of them, and in the box, with one Undo." (pos 20 1026))
  (obj s4c comment "   Play (or Space) plays from the playhead and stops at the end; pressed again, it stops. The position shows bar.beat.tick and minutes:seconds." (pos 20 1044))
  (obj s5 comment "5. Write notes. In the Roll choose Draw and click on a staff: a note; drag to make it longer. Erase takes events out, Select moves them; Snap sets the grid, Q quantizes." (pos 20 1076))
  (obj s5b comment "   Alt+Up and Alt+Down detune the selected notes by a cent (Shift+Alt: ten): the cents are shown by the note. In the List every cell can be typed, the cents too." (pos 20 1094))
  (obj s5c comment "   Under the staves, the score as text (Musil data): change a number there and the roll follows, and the other way round." (pos 20 1112))
  (obj s6 comment "6. Transform with messages. Each changes the selection, or the whole score when nothing is selected: select row Fl takes the flute, select none lets go." (pos 20 1144))
  (obj s6b comment "   A message rewrites the score from outside, so it is not a step of Undo: transpose -2 takes transpose 2 back. The Roll's Transform panel has them as buttons" (pos 20 1162))
  (obj s6c comment "   (each a step of Undo), and Musil as functions (score-transpose! ...). add puts a note in: at, row, pitch, dynamics (a beat long). Closing without saving forgets it all." (pos 20 1180))
  (obj se1 message "select row Fl" (pos 20 1210))
  (obj se2 message "select row Vc" (pos 130 1210))
  (obj se0 message "select none" (pos 240 1210))
  (obj tu message "transpose 2" (pos 335 1210))
  (obj td message "transpose -2" (pos 425 1210))
  (obj iv message invert (pos 520 1210))
  (obj rt message retrograde (pos 580 1210))
  (obj ag message "augment 2" (pos 20 1270))
  (obj dm message "diminish 2" (pos 100 1270))
  (obj qu message "quantize 0.25" (pos 185 1270))
  (obj hu message "humanize 40" (pos 290 1270))
  (obj ad message "add 7.5 Fl C6 f" (pos 385 1270))
  (obj sd1 s t13cmd (pos 20 1240))
  (obj sd1b s t13cmd (pos 20 1300))
  (obj s7 comment "7. The timeline. Click Timeline at the window's top (or open timeline below): the rows are tracks. Fl and Vc hold notes and the motifs, drums two clips of a" (pos 20 1345))
  (obj s7b comment "   sound, bright a lane of points. Drag a clip, drag its edge to trim it; the S key splits the clip at the playhead. M and S in a track's header mute and solo it;" (pos 20 1363))
  (obj s7c comment "   a click on the header shows its strip (gain, pan) in the inspector. The lane's points are messages, each sent at its time to receive t13bright, the filter above:" (pos 20 1381))
  (obj s7d comment "   drag a point higher or later, click on the lane to add one, and listen. A click on a track's name opens what it plays: drums, the sound editor (tutorial 12)." (pos 20 1399))
  (obj s7e comment "   Add puts in tracks, sounds, scores, patch clips (they run in a later version) and lanes; Render... writes the score as a WAV file. Drag a track's lower edge: taller." (pos 20 1417))
  (obj otl message "open timeline" (pos 20 1447))
  (obj oro message "open roll" (pos 120 1447))
  (obj sd2 s t13cmd (pos 20 1477))
  (obj s8 comment "8. Scores inside scores. The faint blocks on the flute's staff are one score placed four times: motif.score (four notes, from examples/15-scores), at 4, 5, 6" (pos 20 1517))
  (obj s8b comment "   and 7 seconds, transposed by 0, 5, 7 and 2. Double-click a block in the Roll: you are inside the motif (the breadcrumb shows where); move a note, and every" (pos 20 1535))
  (obj s8c comment "   placement follows; Esc goes up. In the Timeline a placement is a clip: its stretch and transposition are in the inspector; Make Unique gives one a copy of its own." (pos 20 1553))
  (obj s8d comment "   An edited motif is saved by Save in its window, into motif.score; closing asks: Don't Save leaves the example as it was." (pos 20 1571))
  (obj s9 comment "9. A score from Musil. The code box writes a score and sends it to the box below with (out 1 s): choose a seed, and a walk on a scale fills it." (pos 20 1603))
  (obj s9b comment "   It plays with the tune, on the same clock; another seed, another walk, even while it plays. Double-click the code box: score makes a score, event puts a note in it." (pos 20 1621))
  (obj seed number (pos 20 1650))
  (obj cseed comment "seed: a walk, into the empty score below" (pos 80 1651))
  (obj c code (pos 20 1680)
    (script
      "; a walk on C minor's pentatonic scale, sixteen notes a beat long, as a score sent out of outlet 1"
      "load \"music.mu\""
      "seed in1"
      "var s (score \"t13walk\" 44100)"
      "var scale (list 60 63 65 67 70 72 75 77)"
      "var k 4"
      "each (range 16) (function (i) {"
      "    set k (max 0 (min 7 (+ k (- (floor (* 3 (rand))) 1))))"
      "    event s (* i 0.5) 0.45 (record (list 'kind 'note 'instr \"Ob\" 'midi (getidx scale k) 'dyn \"mp\"))"
      "})"
      "out 1 s"))
  (obj sw score t13walk @size 640 110 (pos 20 1715))
  (obj pn2 prepend note (pos 20 1855))
  (obj poly2 poly~ scorevoice 4 (pos 20 1885))
  (obj vw *~ 0.7 (pos 20 1920))
  (obj out2 dac~ (pos 20 1955))
  (obj s10 comment "10. Where a score lives. These two are kept in the patch: Save the patch and they are saved inside it (see its text with Cmd+T). write puts the tune in a .score" (pos 20 1995))
  (obj s10b comment "   file, Musil data a text editor reads (here in Documents/Moritz); transpose it, then read: it comes back as written. A box named with a file (score mine tune.score)" (pos 20 2013))
  (obj s10c comment "   reads it when the patch opens, and Save in its window writes it. File > Open Score... opens a .score file on its own; Musil reads it with score-read." (pos 20 2031))
  (obj wr message "write ~/Documents/Moritz/t13tune.score" (pos 20 2060))
  (obj rd message "read ~/Documents/Moritz/t13tune.score" (pos 280 2060))
  (obj sd3 s t13cmd (pos 20 2090))
  (obj next comment "Next: tutorial 14, programming with Musil. Examples: 15 scores and 16 timeline (Help > Browser); orchidea's scores in 13 orchestration." (pos 20 2130))
